1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:07,960
History is not always guarded by the sword... sometimes it is written in
ink on parchment and hidden in the middle of the water.

2
00:00:08,017 --> 00:00:15,753
Five hundred years ago, when war and fire were destroying the country's
ancient monasteries, the scholars had only one choice.

3
00:00:15,742 --> 00:00:22,158
Risking their lives, they carried Ethiopia's wisdom, philosophy
and history across to the islands of Lake Tana.

4
00:00:22,342 --> 00:00:28,134
Hidden in dense forest, these islands became
impregnable fortresses of history.

5
00:00:29,942 --> 00:00:36,574
Every page was prepared from goat parchment and written by
hand in ink made from earth and plants.

6
00:00:37,542 --> 00:00:44,798
The paintings on the walls told, vividly, the stories of kings,
the faith of the people and the art of the age.

7
00:00:45,142 --> 00:00:52,974
Because of this, Ethiopia remained the only African country to
keep its own alphabet and written history unbroken.

8
00:00:52,992 --> 00:00:58,688
Like the Abay river, this knowledge has flowed from
generation to generation until it has reached us.

9
00:00:59,592 --> 00:01:07,040
Yesterday our fathers protected our history on parchment; today
we tell it to the world with new technology.

10
00:01:07,192 --> 00:01:10,968
Our history is ours. Let us protect it,
let us tell it.
